      "description": "A genus of secretive, ground-dwelling passerines endemic to Australia, characterised by the prominent bristles around the base of the bill for which they are named. They are stout, long-tailed birds with strong legs and a furtive nature, inhabiting dense heath, sedgeland, and coastal scrub. Their loud, ringing calls are far easier to hear than the birds themselves are to see.",
